export anchor TestModels:
    description:
        When neither `--model` nor the settings give a model, the tool judges
        with its default model, and before the tests run a note lists the models
        of the tool, from the same list `piton agent` shows, and says to choose
        one with `--model`. The run is headless, so it lists them rather than
        asking.

        `--model` with no model lists the models of the agent instead, one on
        each line on stdout, from the same list, like `piton test --agent
        opencode --model`. It runs no tests and exits with 0. An agent that
        lists no models is an error, and the exit code is 1.

        A `--model` value is read as `piton agent` reads it: one of the agent's
        models is that model, and any other value is a search string. The models
        that contain it, ignoring case, are listed, like `piton test --agent
        opencode --model sonnet`, or every model when none contain it. It runs
        no tests and exits with 0. A model from the test settings is never a
        search.
